A||||42||fierosound||rumors of Fiero re-introduction by Pontiac||||1||
Z||000000||fierosound||02-17-2001||10:49 PM||||I got this latest "news" from alt.autos.camaro.firebird newsgroup<P>"There has been more rumors flying out of GMs doors than anyone knows what to do with. First the demise of the camaro and Firebird then the demise of the Oldsmobile line.<P>The latest tops them all. As rumor has it, the Pontiac line is going to re-introduce the Fiero. <P>According to the alligations there will be three versions avalable, The Base form will be a the Fiero G2, which will be available with the Generation 2(hence the name G2) V6 w/ 4 speed auto or 5-speed manual. The other 2 forms will be. The Fiero F1 (Formula 1) and<BR>Fiero SS. <P>Tell me why this seems suspiciously like the Firebird. The F1 and SS will both be available with The LS1 (????) and will both be available with the famous WS6 Perfomance Upgrade. According to GM the F1 will be the only form available with a removabe top and will have head rest roll bars where as the SS is only available w/the basic T-top.<P>The F1 and SS have either 4spd Auto or a six manual. The WS6 will have the Ram Air the tighter suspension 17x9.5 front and 17x11 back. The car is suposidly going to look like it used to except more agressive and<BR>extremely updated. The Biggest difference from the old is that this one is said to have a tranversly mounted engine. <P>According to experts it is going to out handle the Firebird, Camaro, and Mustang and will have almost the same wheelbase as before. And to top it off, if it is released, the price will compete with the Mustang. (I find that hard to believe). In Fact I find this whole thing hard to swallow, considering the Fireos history.<P>But if They have the Balls to do this I will be really interseted to see exactly what happens with it. I was wondering if anyone else got the same E-mail I did. I was also wondering if anyone knows if this is just crap or if its true. we'll see..."<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||02-17-2001||10:59 PM||||I dont know whether I should be happy or not.  Sounds like a totally different car to me.  I like having a unique car.  If they make this new Fiero, they should give it a different name, it just wouldnt be the same thing to me.<P>just my feelings.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||02-17-2001||11:11 PM||||I wonder what the source of THAT rumor was. It's interesting, but it's a complete departure from any speculation that I've heard, previously. (Lotus Elise/Opel Speedster derivative.)<BR>I don't think it will happen, at least not as described above. I don't think the Corvette (or at least the Chevy executives) would be able to handle the competition. <BR>Just my $.02. <BR>Actually, I hope I'm wrong. I'd by a new mid engine LS1 Fiero in a heartbeat.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric||02-18-2001||01:02 AM||||Doesn't leave much breathing room for the Corvette.  I don't think so.||||reg||13
Z||000004||Standard||02-18-2001||01:22 AM||||Well, before the introduction of the ZO6 both the Firebird and the Camaro were almost as fast and sometimes faster than the Corvette, stock for stock.  Still in completely different classes, though.  The Corvette is a true sports/GT car.  Meant for going long distances very fast in comfort.  Camaro/Firebird are musclecars.  Meant for going fast  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  Anyways, the Corvette could sell on image alone... If by some unbelievable miracle those rumours are true, I'll get one even if I have to live with it.<P>------------------<BR>Everybody wants a normal life and a cool car.. <B>Most people settle for the car</B><P>I'm not dumb.  I just have a command of thoroughly useless information<BR>        <BR>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd<BR>AIM: SavedByJebus    -- you'll understand if you watch The Simpsons :D||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||02-18-2001||02:09 AM||||I haven't heard this one, but I'd like to hear more.  Personally, if it's not mid-engined, IMHO, it's not a Fiero.  Beyond that, I'd like to see what they come up with. I always though Pontiac dropped the ball when they cancelled the Fiero (duh). If they'd hung on a few more years, with the sport compact market just beginning to emerge, the Fiero could have been a tremendous success.  Look at the Miata, MR-2, and god knows how many Civics and Eclipse's.  There's a lot of missed market share for the Fiero out there.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Haze_Performance||02-18-2001||04:17 AM||||Well it would be kinda cool but....... I can safely say that the Fiero will <B><I>NEVER</I></B> come back in <B><I>ANY</I></B> form. <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif"> </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery</A>||||reg||6
Z||000007||MontanaFiero||02-18-2001||04:35 AM||||fierosound wrote:<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>The Biggest difference from the old is that this one is said to have a tranversly mounted engine. <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Isn't that what's in the Fiero's <I>now</I>?  They certainly aren't a <I>traditional</I> rear wheel drive.  Are they trying to say the new fiero will be a front wheel drive? If so, then  it's NOT a Fiero!<P>------------------<BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- project &lt;&lt;<p>[This message has been edited by MontanaFiero (edited 02-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierosound||02-18-2001||05:18 AM||||I believe what they meant was a "north-south" engine placement, ala Ferrari/Lamborghini/Pantera etc., as opposed to an "east-west" configuration we have due to using essentially a front-wheel drive powertrain.  That would necessitate a ZF trans-axle of some type.  No point arguing about it though, This may never see the light of day - if it does, it'll be $29,000 minumum!<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000009||bHooper||02-18-2001||09:46 AM||||personally, i don't think they will ever make another Fiero.  it would be like a steamship line naming their next boat <I>Titanic</I> or [i]Lucitania[/a], or some mother naming their kid Adolf... <B>it just ain't gonna happen!</B><P>now done to details... $29,000 wouldn't be a bad price at all, our cars were between $13-18,000, 13 years ago, so dollar to dollar, that would be a good deal!  i also don't see gm installing a <B>Longitudinal</B> (north south) engine in a "cheap" mid-engine car... maybe if they were to ever actually produce a mid-engine 'vette.<P>there is a good side io gm building a "new fiero", they could posssibly start making parts for the old cars again.<P>i would love to be wrong, and certainly would buy one (no matter what the price) but i doubt it will ever happen.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000010||pHoOl||02-18-2001||10:36 AM||||I'll give my $.02<P>I have heard that one of the reasons that the Fiero never got the Twin Turbo V6 was because of too much pressure from Chevy.  It would have spanked the Vette.  <P>Next, unless they were to make the car a bit longer, i don't see the north south engine mount being benificial.  It would end up putting some of the weight behind the axle, which would make it a rear mounted engine, not mid.  I've heard that rear engine cars handle like crap.<P>Third, there is no way that Chevy would let pontiac do this again, especially if the car was cheaper than the vette, and had a vette in it.<P><BR>Disclaimer:  I am by no means an expert, I am just speaking from the views of my 19 years of existance.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Songman||02-18-2001||10:47 AM||||Rear engine cars don't exactly handle like crap, you just have to get used to handling them a little different. I learned that the first time I got my 911 sideways!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Sillhouette.com||02-18-2001||11:06 AM||||GM has to bring something back instead of the Camaro, Firebird and Oldsmobile lineup. You just can't erase two successfull lineups and a moderate one and still expect to make money.  So something will have to arrive to fill the void.  The Corvette is a Piece of Crap IMHO.  Most racers disconnect the famous drive by wire system because it takes away from the seat of the pants feeling.  If anyone ever buys a Corvette it's because the name.  Certainly not because of handling or power.  There are much quicker and nicer cars out there thant the corvette.  M5 comes to mind right now.  The point of this is that GM cannot assume that the Corvette lineup will be able to fill the void. I hope it's the Fiero that gets resurrected.  I will certainly buy an SS model maybe two and of course supercharge the living daylights out of it.  <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000013||LZeitgeist||02-18-2001||12:05 PM||||I doubt it will happen. On the other hand, I hope to hell that I'm wrong.<P>But, if it's not two-seater, mid-engine, rear-wheel-drive, it's not a Fiero.<P>Besides, Suzuki now owns the name 'Fiero'. Pontiac would have to add the re-purchase of the name to the price of production.<P>I don't think the Corvette lobby will allow it to happen, though... unless Pontiac replaces the Fierbird line-up with the new Fiero. And you all know how well *that* will fly with the general public - to them, the Fiero was a failed-attempt bastard child, and for it to take the place of the almighty TransAm would be a slap in the face... there'd be mass hysteria in the performance car market. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Formula88||02-18-2001||12:26 PM||||Even if a Fiero-esque car gets introduced by Pontiac (say the Opel Speedster, for example), I don't think it would be named Fiero.  Too much bad publicity in the general public's eye.  Hopefully they'll make antother fun car similar to the Fiero, and I'd love for it to be called Fiero, but it won't happen. ||||reg||6
Z||000015||JBGehling||02-18-2001||02:03 PM||||I can sum this up in 4 words: no chance in hell<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>dang rumors...||||reg||1
Z||000016||Pontiaddict||02-18-2001||03:29 PM||||I doubt that will happen. If it does, it certainly won't have an LS1 though a v8 wouldn't be out of the question. Possibly a 4L ohc but not a N* based motor.<P>Now for a free psychic reading....<BR> I expect the Camaro to be replaced by a more production like (aka crappier) Nomad. Then expect the new Firebird replacement to be based on the same platform but more carlike.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000017||jerpro||02-18-2001||05:15 PM||||SO WHAT IF THE CORVETTE DIES!!!!!!!<BR>Corvette, just like any other car has to leave room for better and faster cars to go by. Corvette has had it's moments of glory.<BR>Now.... STEP DOWN!!!!!!<BR>sorry had to vent<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||lou_dias||02-18-2001||05:26 PM||||There's too many damn pessemists on this board.<BR>If it's a mid-engine pontiac with 2 seats, a stick shift and does 0-60 in under 5.5 (with some room for improvement) seconds, I'm buying it.  Speedster or not.<BR>Anyone see a MATCHBOX car called the Pontiac Salsa? WTF is that?  it looks awesome.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Black88GT||02-18-2001||08:16 PM||||Silhoutte.com, were you joking when you said no one buys Vette's for the handling and power?  Please tell me you were.  Also the M5 is double the price of the Z06, probably more by the time the BMW dealer adds on their extra "dealer" fee's.  <P>You say there are "much quicker" cars then the Vette.  Name one thats a second faster to 60 and costs less then 100 grand.  Now try to name one that does a Qtr. in less time then a Z06 and costs under 50 grand.  <BR>For the money you can not buy a better sportscar.<P>Now about the Fiero resurection, it doesn't make any sense at all.  Why would they kill the f-body, then bring out basically another F-body with a FIERO nameplate?!?!  The Fiero name badge is DEAD FOREVER.  Just the mention of the word to many mechanics/people in general brings the misconceptions of "fiery deathtrap" no matter what you tell them.  People are too dumb to change their outlook on a car after its reputation has been totally destroyed 5 times over, no matter what you do.  Americans are too busy in their "safe and gas efficient" SUV's to worry about a cheap Sports Cars.<P>Also, it says "The car is suposidly going to look like it used to except more agressive and extremely updated."  Well think about that for a second.  How can it look like it used to while being extremely updated and more agressively styled.  <P>The more I read it the more I think some 14 year old kid is spreading rumors (notice the bad grammar and spelling errors?)<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">               <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">               <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 02-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||p4n1c||02-18-2001||10:03 PM||||Oldsmobile and moderate don't belong in the same sentence.  Olds has been around since I think 1896.  It's one of the oldest nameplates.  <P>If noone's ever heard of it, the 1987 Oldsmobile Aerotech.<P>•1987: The Aerotech, powered by a modified Oldsmobile Quad 4(4 cylinder) engine, sets a land speed record of 257 mph(411kph).<P>The fastest internal combustion engine ever made. Pulled that from: <BR> <A HREF="http://popularmechanics.com/popmech/auto3/0012AUNCWFAM.html" TARGET=_blank>http://popularmechanics.com/popmech/auto3/0012AUNCWFAM.html</A> <P>The Quad4 production is about 180hp with the high output engine.<P>The newer Aerotech broke speed-endurance records set by Mercedes Benz using a production 4.0 Aurora V8.<P>So let's not call it moderate.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 02-18-2001).]||||reg||1
